# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
# The console font's hand-drawn glyphs (DESIGN D28 section 6), Zenix's own: the three boxes (glyphs 0-2 of every font),
# the terminal symbols CP437 lacks, and a few marks of ordinary text. Read by tools/mkconfont.py. Each glyph is a line
# "U+XXXX name" (or "box", "wide-left", "wide-right") and eight lines of eight pixels, # set and . clear, bit 7 left.
# Drawn for the console's 8 x 8 cell (a hires pixel is about twice as tall as it is wide): the light box lines of the
# generated set are at columns 3-4 and row 4, so symbols that sit on a line (the arrows, the result corner) meet it.

box
